menu "Honch SDK"

config HONCH_ERROR_TRACKING
    bool "Enable automatic error tracking"
    default y
    help
        Compile Honch automatic error tracking support. Disable this to strip
        the SDK-owned fault snapshot and $error emission path from firmware.

config HONCH_CRASH_SYMBOLICATION
    bool "Enable crash symbolication context"
    depends on HONCH_ERROR_TRACKING
    default y
    help
        Include firmware build IDs and raw crash addresses from ESP-IDF ELF
        coredump summaries so Honch can resolve function and source lines after
        matching symbols are uploaded.

        When the ELF coredump-to-flash options are also enabled
        (CONFIG_ESP_COREDUMP_ENABLE_TO_FLASH + CONFIG_ESP_COREDUMP_DATA_FORMAT_ELF)
        and a "coredump" partition exists, the SDK additionally streams the raw
        coredump image off flash to Honch after a crash and erases it once Honch
        acknowledges the upload. See the README "Crash coredump upload" section.

config HONCH_LIFECYCLE_EVENTS
    bool "Enable automatic lifecycle events"
    default y
    help
        Emit $device_boot, $firmware_update, and $device_shutdown
        automatically. Disable to compile these out; the firmware-version
        baseline is still maintained so re-enabling never spuriously re-emits.

config HONCH_SESSIONS
    bool "Enable session tracking"
    default y
    help
        Emit $session_start / $session_end via the session API. Disable to
        compile the session-tracking code out; the session_id event field is
        always retained.

config HONCH_BATTERY
    bool "Enable battery telemetry"
    default y
    help
        Emit the $battery_level auto-property and the $battery_low edge event.
        Disable to compile the battery sampling/emission out (the public
        battery config fields remain).

endmenu
